WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:26.160
Chapter 13. White paper v1.1, Claim Registry, and boundaries. White paper v1.1 is a bilingual application-layer summary with 22 pages, 9 tables, and 3 figures. It summarizes 12 claims and adds a construct-boundary figure; detailed tests and failure conditions remain governed by repository documents.

2
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:47.505
Compared with v1.0, v1.1 adds a construct-boundary chapter, a third figure, and a Claim Registry summary table, growing from 19 to 22 pages. Counts were verified from the actual PDF and DOCX structures, not estimated by hand.

3
00:00:47.825 --> 00:01:10.110
MI-C001 through MI-C012 cover definition, meta-layer relation, three dimensions, spectrum, multi-scale coordination, recursive review, and layer effects. New claims start at MI-C100; existing IDs are never renumbered, and withdrawn claims keep their IDs.

4
00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:36.424
The white paper does not replace the canon. Theoretical citations return to canon sections, H1–H18, or Appendix D.7. Engineering citations need a claim ID, evidence level, status, and failure condition. The boundary map distinguishes this directional-regulation construct from same-named fields without claiming exclusivity.

5
00:01:36.744 --> 00:01:45.367
22 pages: actual PDF page count.

6
00:01:45.687 --> 00:01:53.775
9 tables: actual DOCX table count.

7
00:01:54.095 --> 00:02:02.642
3 figures: actual DOCX inline-shape count.

8
00:02:02.962 --> 00:02:13.265
12 claims: summary; detailed governance in docs/claims.md.

9
00:02:13.585 --> 00:02:28.061
